WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.499 --> 00:00:05.240
 In music, you're basically
having a conversation.

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:06.946
Here's a question.

00:00:06.946 --> 00:00:09.730
Here's an answer.

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:14.280
Ooh, bit of a dodgy
question here.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.770
I am convinced that I have
no idea how to do your movie.

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:19.710
It's always a blank
piece of paper.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.391
I can tell you everything you
need to know in one word--

00:00:26.391 --> 00:00:26.890
story.

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:33.740
All of it [INAUDIBLE],, set
designer, actor, writer,

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:35.850
composer-- we try
to create worlds.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:39.070
Sherlock is a score
anybody could do.

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:41.320
One microphone on a laptop.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:43.150
Ideas are not limited by budget.

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:47.390
The creative process
takes place in your head.

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:50.060
The interesting ideas
come from some kid

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:52.010
in a garage in the Bronx.

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:54.170
You just need to
break through the myth

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:56.840
that you can't create
a great Hollywood

00:00:56.840 --> 00:01:00.690
blockbuster on an iPad because
if you [INAUDIBLE] story,

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:02.180
you can do whatever
you want to do.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.950
I like your writing in D, and
it's nice that if you go from--

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:20.570
[MUSIC PLAYING] it's satisfying.

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:23.300
For "Batman," four French
horns on the right,

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:26.450
four French horns on the left,
and they're up in a gallery,

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:28.420
up way above the orchestra.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:30.880
Two notes, but the
amount of expressiveness

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:32.066
you can put into them.

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:38.890
This is a musician's life.

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:41.470
Everybody tells you not to
do it and get a real job.

00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:44.000
When all is said and done,
and we've filled the highest

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.549
highrises, and we built
the fastest machines,

00:01:46.549 --> 00:01:48.340
there's still going to
be room for somebody

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:51.530
to tell you a story or somebody
to write you a piece of music.

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:53.840
The seconds of your
life are ticking away.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:57.040
If somebody tells you that
there's a rule, break it.

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:00.310
That's the only thing
that move things forward.

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:04.560
I'm Hans Zimmer, and
this is my Masterclass.

